Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:46:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1050/1286] The player hears FLAC: listen.flac written at save,
 served with native seeking

1053 (Viktor): a WAV take gets listen.flac beside audio.wav when it is saved
(the built-in lossless encoder, about 74 % of the bytes at 24 bit); a take
older than that gets it at its first listen. GET /library/listen serves it as
a file, so Range and seeking are the server's own; an MP3 take, or a take
whose FLAC cannot be made, is served as it is. The page plays /library/listen
and downloads /library/audio (the WAV, as before); a server without the
route falls back to the WAV for the session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
